# Trivy findings that are deliberate here, with the reason. Anything not listed
# below is expected to fail CI — do not add entries without a justification.

# DS002 / DS-0002 — "Image user should not be 'root'"
#
# Both spellings are listed deliberately: Trivy renamed this check's ID between
# releases (DS002 in 0.58.x, DS-0002 in newer builds). Listing only one makes
# the suppression silently stop working the day the scanner is upgraded.
#
# All four images intentionally start as root, and three of them cannot do
# otherwise:
#
#   worker_image/, worker_image_ovpn/ — the startup script must be root to
#     create the tunnel interface, replace the default route and install the
#     iptables kill-switch. A USER directive would break the no-leak guarantee
#     outright. It does not *stay* root: aria2, the only process that handles
#     untrusted torrent data, is dropped to PUID:PGID with setpriv once the
#     tunnel is up and the firewall is armed (see SECURITY.md, "Downloads are
#     not root-owned"), and the container runs with cap_drop: ALL plus a
#     five-capability add-back.
#
#   docker/Dockerfile.api — needs to read the bind-mounted project directory
#     and talk to the Docker socket proxy. Worth revisiting: it is the one image
#     where a non-root USER is plausible, tracked in AUDIT-RESPONSE.md.
#
#   docker/Dockerfile.web — no longer applies: it uses nginx-unprivileged and
#     runs as uid 101. Listed only because api/ and the mules still need root.
DS002
DS-0002
